{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And he shall sprinkle upon the one being purified seven times</b> — corresponding to seven things for which negaim come upon a person; over them he sprinkles seven times." "<b>And he shall send the bird</b> — a hint that the tzara'at shall fly away from him. One bird slaughtered — thus tzara'at shall not come again. And one sent for him — that if he continues to do evil, the tzara'at shall return like the sent bird."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {1 "Reading צפוד (bound/tied) as the word written in the source for the sent bird; the logic turns on the bird being let go yet able to return."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:24.330966746Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}